---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party data and assets (NOT covered by the MIT licence above)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT licence applies to the source code in this repository only. Bundled
and runtime-fetched data carry their own licences:

* srv/static/austria.json — simplified Austrian ADM0 outline, derived from
  geoBoundaries gbOpen / BEV. CC BY-SA 4.0. Modified (Douglas-Peucker
  simplification).
* redlist.csv, redlist_curated.json — European Red List of species,
  IUCN / European Environment Agency. Attribution required; see
  https://www.eea.europa.eu/legal/copyright
* srv/static/fonts/ — "Press Start 2P" (CodeMan38) and "VT323"
  (Peter Hull), SIL Open Font License 1.1.
* Cadastre, LiDAR, land-use and municipality data fetched at runtime:
  BEV – Bundesamt für Eich- und Vermessungswesen (CC BY 4.0, bearbeitet),
  Statistik Austria (CC BY 4.0), EEA Natura 2000, RIS (CC BY 4.0),
  ESA WorldCover 2021 (CC BY 4.0), Hansen GFC-2024 v1.12 and Harris et al.
  forest carbon flux via Global Forest Watch (CC BY 4.0),
  OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL, display only).
* Agricultural layers fetched at runtime via farm-subsidies-austria:
  AMA / BML INVEKOS Schläge (field blocks) and Hofstellen (farmsteads, hashed
  ids only) from INSPIRE / data.gv.at, and municipal subsidy aggregates from
  the AMA Transparenzdatenbank — CC BY 4.0, aggregated, no personal data.
* Forestry data fetched at runtime via holzeinschlag-at: Statistik Austria
  Holzeinschlag (CC BY 4.0), LK Holzmarktberichte via
  preise.agrarforschung.at (model values).
* Water data fetched at runtime via groundwater-at: BML eHYD groundwater
  levels, gauges and stations, Wasserschatz Österreich 2021, WISE / EEA water
  quality and WFD status, Copernicus EDO drought index (CC BY 4.0);
  water flow paths from MERIT Hydro / MERIT-Basins via mghydro.com
  (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 — display only, non-commercial).
* Terrain layers fetched at runtime via srtm-lidar-at: hillshade tiles,
  tree apices and building heights derived from the BEV ALS model
  (CC BY 4.0, bearbeitet); srtm-lidar-at attribution list at
  https://srtm-lidar-at.exe.xyz:8000/api/v1/attribution
  Full attribution list: docs/grants/data-licensing-check.md and the
  in-app Impressum.
